2026-10-02T15:46:47.7969414Z   ok   naive timestamps carry one offset (None) and keep learning
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7969423Z 
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7969622Z -- v4.0.4 — negative-mean initial guess
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7969864Z   ok   a positive-mean horizon gets the historical formula bit for bit
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7970114Z   ok   all-negative prices: the cheapest (most negative) step starts highest
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7970527Z   ok   and the guess is monotone in price rank, inside the same 0.2-1.0 band
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7970744Z   ok   the un-guarded formula really did invert on this input
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7970985Z   ok   a near-zero mean takes the rank path instead of saturating the clip
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7971233Z   ok   sun entirely past the solve horizon moves no warm-start weight (#933)
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7971461Z   ok   the same sun inside the horizon does discount (#933 null control)
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7971652Z   ok   a zero-step lookahead leaves every weight at one (#933)
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7971660Z 
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7971873Z -- v4.0.4 — grid-fee magnitude repair issue
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7972168Z   ok   max_abs_component finds the öre-as-SEK rule and names its source
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7972327Z   ok   an inactive layer has nothing to warn about
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7972542Z   ok   entity mode inspects the live value, rules mode ignores it
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7972824Z   ok   a 25 SEK/kWh rule — öre in a SEK field — raises the repair issue
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7973042Z   ok   warn-only: the plan still prices with exactly what was typed
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7973260Z   ok   the issue is raised once per offending value, not every cycle
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7973478Z   ok   a corrected configuration clears the issue on the next cycle
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7973718Z   ok   0.25 SEK/kWh — the value that was meant — raises nothing
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7974011Z   ok   a fee sensor publishing öre trips the same issue, attributed to it
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7974263Z   ok   a stored negative rule raises the sign notice, attributed to the rules
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7974501Z   ok   warn-only: the plan still prices with the negative value it was given
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7974735Z   ok   the sign notice is raised once per offending value, not every cycle
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7975118Z   ok   and a negative rate of ordinary size is not mistaken for a magnitude slip
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7975314Z   ok   correcting the sign clears the notice on the next cycle
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7975608Z   ok   a fee sensor publishing a negative value trips the same notice, attributed to it
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7975879Z   ok   the magnitude notice and the sign notice are independent: -25 raises both
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7976002Z   ok   0.25 SEK/kWh raises neither
2026-10-02T15:46:47.7976010Z 
