2026-10-02T15:50:33.2193740Z   ok   the grace the repair's text calls half an hour is thirty minutes
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2194374Z   ok   a blind release (unload) writes OFF to every owned switch unread, and keeps only the record whose OFF failed
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2195153Z   ok   control: the boost-start edge turns the switch ON exactly once across three commanded cycles, and owns it
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2195845Z   ok   …and the ownership is in the cycle's store, where a restart reads it
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2196471Z   ok   …and the boost close turns it OFF exactly once, and ownership ends when it reads off
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2197537Z   ok   with the optimizer off a legionella action still current never turns the disinfection switch on (null control above: on, it does)
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2198258Z   ok   the boost bound closes the window and turns the switch OFF once
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2198891Z   ok   a boost the bound closed is not switched back on by the same command
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2199480Z   ok   …and once the plan has moved on, the next commanded boost turns it on
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2199967Z   ok   disabling disinfection during a boost turns the switch OFF
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2200446Z   ok   no ON while this cycle's mode reading blocks hot water, logged once
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2201073Z   ok   …and the ON goes out on the first cycle the mode allows hot water, with no solve between
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2201663Z   ok   a switch that was already on is left alone through a whole boost and after it
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2202149Z   ok   an idle control install writes nothing, not even OFF
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2202595Z   ok   a failed write raises a non-persistent repair naming the switch
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2203144Z   ok   …the next cycle retries the ON, and its success clears the repair
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2203634Z   ok   a failed OFF at the close is retried on the next idle cycle, once
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2204196Z   ok   an OFF the switch ignored is re-sent while it still reads on, and stops once it reads off
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2204841Z   ok   an owned switch that goes unavailable is waited for, then turned OFF when it is back on
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2205449Z   ok   restart mid-boost: the next run turns off the switch the last one turned on
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2205976Z   ok   …and once it read off, the store no longer names it
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2206480Z   ok   reload into observe mid-boost: the owned switch is turned OFF and never back ON
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2207378Z   ok   reload onto another switch mid-boost: the new switch ON, the old one OFF, in the same cycle
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2208243Z   ok   renamed switch: the old record is kept through the grace, then dropped with a persistent repair naming it, and nothing is written blind
2026-10-02T15:50:33.2209226Z   ok   …and the drop is in the store, so a restart does not resurrect the record
